      "message": "In an auth callback I added this code:\n\n```\n\tgo func() {\n\t\tfor {\n\t\t\terr :\u003d preConn.SendAuthBanner(\"test\\r\\n\")\n\t\t\tif err !\u003d nil {\n\t\t\t\tfmt.Printf(\"unable to send the banner: %v\\n\", err)\n\t\t\t\treturn\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}()\n\tpreConn.SendAuthBanner(\"initial banner\\r\\n\")\n\ttime.Sleep(200 * time.Millisecond)\n\treturn nil,nil\n```\n\nand I was able to send a banner after `msgUserAuthSuccess`. The `ssh` CLI fails like this\n\n```\ndispatch_protocol_error: type 53 seq 21548\ndispatch_protocol_error: type 53 seq 21549\nConnection to 127.0.0.1 closed by remote host.\nclient_loop: send disconnect: Broken pipe\n```\n\nSo this is a fatal error.\nI think we should use a mutex to make sure the `writePacket` requests for `userAuthBannerMsg` and `msgUserAuthSuccess` are properly serialized. What do you think about?",
